places.contents:
The basin (layer 7): black crust 1-2 m above a lobed lava pool, with the river running into it and lavacracks scattered all round.

Things, relative to the place:
- steam vents: smoke at [-40,-40] { h 40, n 8, color '#b8bcc2', spread 0.8 } and at [70,0] { h 30, n 7, spread 0.7 }, both on dry crust;
- wrecksmoke at [-60,0] { h 14, r 1.4, n 10 };
- grove(41,12,18,60,['lavarock'],[1.5,4.5]), down from 14 rocks.

- nevarrotower at [0,0], yaw 2.3 (the S3 'building on the hill over the streets');
- kmast at [9,-5] (mast, dish, red beacon);
- lamp at [-7,7] (dark post).

From here you see the whole town in its bowl, the river and the volcano. Climbed from the North Lane: 240 m, normal 0.70.

scores.notes:
It has the strongest landforms:
- a 393 m volcano 25 degrees up at 690 m, only 21% fogged;
- a close mountain ring;
- a 63 m escarpment;
- a lava river and a lava field covering 3.7% of the walkable disc.

Its numbers are honest: my probe gives exactly its -1.9 to 263.6 m range and 1,806 too-steep cells. The cantina stays at [140,-90] with yaw 0.300, the door is on h 9, and all quest spots are flat.

Canon wins:
- the keelboat at the Charon tunnel mouth (Chapter 8);
- four parked TIEs at the base (canon has four Outland TIEs);
- New Republic X-wings in the yard (Season 2, Chapter 12);
- the Clan Mudhorn homestead (Season 3, Chapter 24).

Canon misses:
- 'turret' is the Rebel DF.9 from Hoth (catalog/ice.js:16), placed at an Imperial base;
- a lambda shuttle at the base;
- 'Trexler's run' is fanon (the Trexler 906 is the Marauder they escaped in, not a place);
- 'the Fingers' are Lothal's lothspire builder recoloured.

Other problems:
- Lava is a harmless 1.3 m 'wade'. scene.js:218 excludes lava from wading, so the player just walks on the riverbed inside the glowing plane, and in 110 basin cells the camera goes under it.
- The terrain build measured 1,836 ms on the high tier and 717 ms on the small tier. It runs synchronously in scene.js:214-215, so that is 14 times today's time and more than 3 times Tatooine's. The cause is 14 layers, 128 flats and 55 pits.
- nevarro.site.mjs has no life, quests, zones or flyovers, so its life moves exist only in prose.
- The town is 16 house fronts against the walls of a 44 m bowl, so it is less dense than the landmarks town.

bestIdeasToGraft:
Take the player proposal's whole play layer:
- you land facing the gate;
- each about-text points to the next stop;
- per-place crew lines;
- Greef as the real 'greef' crew figure instead of 'villager';
- Kuiil and Cara Dune at the Crest camp;
- the Client's safe house;
- the scout troopers' can gag;
- the 'forge' quest (a `use` step after the puck) at the covert.

Keep the landmarks discipline:
- new layers go only at the end of the list (noise seeds stay put);
- scatter order is kept and replayed with the scene's rng;
- exit cones out of every steep lava bed;
- abs-height placement for portals and the base.

mistakes:
All three: no sequel content; every engine feature they rely on exists:
- deck with hw, hd, depth and color (props/core.js:827);
- parked with a url falling back to the built version (placer.js:247);
- pitch on any thing;
- scatter `clear`;
- every life kind.

All quest coordinates sit on flat ground on both grid tiers. All three still break the +10% baseline rule against today's 87 draw calls and 0.94M triangles, and use the TIE/ln model where canon has Outland TIEs.
